Affected component: Source NAT on the border router r1 (iptables NAT/POSTROUTING). Mechanism: PC1’s traffic to public IPs is forwarded through the campus and reaches r1, but leaves r1 toward ISPA with an RFC1918 source (10.x). ISPA has no route back to 10.x, so replies are dropped. That makes all outbound TCP connections from clients time out, while r1 itself can reach the Internet (its packets have public source IPs). Localization: Device r1, WAN-facing interface eth2 (203.0.113.2) toward ISPA. Evidence: 
